'''Hype Trains''' is a community gifting feature in which users in an instance collectively send [[Special:MyLanguage/VRC+|VRC+]] gift drops within a time limit to reach a shared goal and unlock personnal and/or global rewards during specific events.

==Overview==
The Hype Train was first introduced during the [[Special:MyLanguage/Pride Month 2026|Pride Month 2026]] event. A Hype Train starts when the [[Special:MyLanguage/Instances|instance]] receives a total two gift drops from users within the timer window. A Hype Train can be started depending on the event in any or specific world and in any instance. Each gift drop that is sent resets the timer, and the Hype Train ends if the timer runs out before the goal is reached.

When a Hype Train is completed, users who are in the instance during the active hype train will receive the rewards.

==Behavior==
===Indicator & UI===
During an active hype train, instances showcased a "train" icon indicating the a hype train is active. It also shows the amount of gift drops that were sent out of how many is needed.

Within the instance, active hype trains displayed a custom [[Special:MyLanguage/Quick Menu|Quick Menu]] widget showcasing the amount of gifts sent, gifters, personal contributions, and time remaining. Ended hype trains showed an alternate version. Depending on the event [[Special:MyLanguage/VRCat|VRCat]] will be displayed according to the theme. Clicking it will make VRCat comment on the ongoing hype train. 

The [[Special:MyLanguage/HUD|HUD]] also displays custom elements. During an active hype train, it showcases the amount of gifts sent and time remaining. When a hype train is completed, it showcases an element displaying "Hype Train complete: reward unlocked!".

===Goal & timer===
For a Hype Train to be completed, users must reach a set goal of gift drops. In addition, the goal must be completed within the time limit of the last gift drop sent.

Each gift drop sent resets the timer back to it's original state. 

The goal & timer of the hype train changes each events. In some cases, like during the Holiday Event 2026, the hype train may feature different goals, each rewarding different rewards when reached.

===Reward===
When a Hype Train is completed, users who are in the instance will receive the designated reward.

